{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_5>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <tuple>\n#include <functional>\n#include <iterator>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nstruct Candidate {\n    i64 a;\n    i64 b;\n};\n\ninline pair<i64, i64> get_bounds(int x, int y, int b) {\n    i64 num = static_cast<i64>(b) * x;\n    i64 lo = num / y;\n    i64 hi = (num + y - 1) / y;\n    return {lo, hi};\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    vector<Candidate> pool;\n    pool.reserve(2 * n);\n    \n    for (int b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n        auto [lo, hi] = get_bounds(x, y, b);\n        pool.push_back({lo, b});\n        pool.push_back({hi, b});\n    }\n    \n    auto error = [&](const Candidate& c) -> i64 {\n        return llabs(static_cast<i64>(x) * c.b - c.a * y);\n    };\n    \n    auto cmp = [&](const Candidate& lhs, const Candidate& rhs) {\n        i64 el = error(lhs);\n        i64 er = error(rhs);\n        if (el != er) return el < er;\n        if (lhs.b != rhs.b) return lhs.b < rhs.b;\n        return lhs.a < rhs.a;\n    };\n    \n    nth_element(pool.begin(), pool.begin(), pool.end(), cmp);\n    auto best = pool[0];\n    \n    cout << best.a << \"/\" << best.b << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_5>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    x = int(data[0])\n    y = int(data[1])\n    n = int(data[2])\n    \n    pool = []\n    \n    def get_bounds(x, y, b):\n        num = b * x\n        lo = num // y\n        hi = (num + y - 1) // y\n        return (lo, hi)\n    \n    for b in range(1, n + 1):\n        lo, hi = get_bounds(x, y, b)\n        pool.append((lo, b))\n        pool.append((hi, b))\n    \n    def error(c):\n        a, b = c\n        return abs(x * b - a * y)\n    \n    def cmp_key(c):\n        return (error(c), c[1], c[0])\n    \n    # Find the minimum element based on the comparison criteria\n    best = min(pool, key=cmp_key)\n    \n    print(f\"{best[0]}/{best[1]}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.893881360767409e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.04132365435361862, -0.029870636761188507, -0.043030284345149994, -0.5759899616241455, -0.001430798671208322, -0.14269007742404938, -0.02036074921488762, -0.5232351422309875, -1.823885577323381e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.4024292528629303, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.023333145305514336, -6.246371776796877e-05, -0.006005812902003527, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.00021419614495243877, -2.062299427052494e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.2930335998535156, -0.00038044367101974785, -5.722029527532868e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.172316494077677e-06, 0.0, -5.9604627722